research_rationale:
EO:11741 (signed 1973-10-15; 38 FR 28809, Federal Register of October 17, 1973) directs each Federal department and agency of the executive branch to use the official American Revolution Bicentennial symbol on publications, envelopes, stationery and other appropriate documents to the extent permitted by law and deemed appropriate (section 1), permits one-color or three-color use (section 2), and provides that use of the symbol pursuant to the order "shall continue through 
D ecem ber 31, 1976." (section 3). Identity: the registered original is the Federal Register printing in jobs/fr-originals; number, date and subject agree with the census register. Inventory: I confirm the dossier's three scopes, sections 1, 2 and 3, as the complete operative text; the recitals are not commands. Section 3 fixes the period of use, so section 1 and section 2, which govern that use, end with it on 1976-12-31, recorded inclusive (the text says the use continues through that date); the exclusive reading is 1977-01-01 as the day the period has run out. Section 3 is itself the duration term and ends on the same date. Searches, chosen after reading their coverage notes (all complete, none with a coverage warning): the U.S. Code search (release point 119-121, citations of the order by number in statute text and notes; edition current through 2026-10-09) recorded 0 hits; the eCFR point-in-time search as of 2026-10-14 with GovInfo CFR bulk XML recorded 0 hits; the Federal Register catalog disposition-note search (1937 onward) recorded 0 hits for this order. I also searched every held order text (the Cruden held-text search, 33118 readable files) for the order's number; the only held texts that cite it are its own Federal Register printing. I found no held order that revokes or amends it.
Member checks: {"earlier_end_check":"Own terms give the only ending found: section 3's period of use through 1976-12-31. The held-text number search finds only the order's own printing, and the machine searches record 0 U.S. Code, 0 eCFR and 0 Federal Register catalog hits, so no earlier revocation, supersession or amendment is held.","independent_command_check":"Section 1 directs agency use of a symbol adopted by the American Revolution Bicentennial Commission and section 2 allows its colors; neither creates a continuing duty beyond the period set in section 3, and the order assigns no function to the Commission.","savings_check":"Publications, envelopes, stationery and documents that already bore the symbol are accrued completed acts; the order continues no duty after 1976-12-31.","scope_check":"Sections 1 and 2 govern the use of the symbol and section 3 limits that use in time, so all three scopes end on the date section 3 fixes; no held text amends any section."}
